            "content": "<!-- qualor:reply 84e3a014-ae9b-4b62-8436-fa6e00005388 -->\n**AI review** · reply\n\nThe rule flags empty functions because an empty body usually means something was left unfinished, or that the author meant to do something and forgot. A reader cannot tell a deliberate no-op from a missing implementation, and that makes the code harder to maintain. In ` probe/item-21-20261124112507.js `, ` emptyHandler ` on line 2 is exported and has a body with nothing in it, and the search of the repository finds no other use of it. Fix it in one of three ways. If the function should do work, implement that work. If it is meant as a deliberate no-op, such as a default callback, keep it and add a comment inside the braces that says why it does nothing, since a comment satisfies the rule. If nothing needs it, delete it. Because it is exported, check for external callers before you remove it.",
