            "content": "<!-- qualor:issue 1b335464-00d3-4ddb-8c96-fa6e0000ac38 -->\n**AI review** · High · Logic · likely · ` ai:logic `\n\n**canDeleteAccount returns true for non-admins, inverting the documented admin-only rule**\n\nThe doc comment says only administrators may delete accounts, but ` !user.isAdmin ` is true for every non-admin and false for administrators. Any caller that uses this as the deletion gate lets ordinary users delete accounts and blocks admins. The condition should be ` user.isAdmin `. The function also throws a TypeError when ` user ` is null or undefined, so the fix should return false for a missing user.\n\nAssumes: Callers use the return value directly as the permission check for account deletion.\n\n```suggestion\nexport const canDeleteAccount = (user) => Boolean(user && user.isAdmin);\n```\n\n[View in Qualor](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/6d581179-0227-4214-891e-fa6e0000c552/issues/1b335464-00d3-4ddb-8c96-fa6e0000ac38)",
